      "text": "Given the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\), we know that \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of this polynomial. By Vieta's formulas, we have the following relationships for the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 5x^2 + 6x - 9 = 0\\):\n\n\\[\nr + s + t = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 6,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 9.\n\\]\n\nWe need to compute the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\). First, let's rewrite the expression in terms of the roots:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s} = \\frac{r s^2}{t} + \\frac{s t^2}{r} + \\frac{t r^2}{s}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity \\(r s t = 9\\) to express the terms in the numerator in terms of the roots. Notice that:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r s^2}{t} = \\frac{r s \\cdot s}{t} = \\frac{s (rs)}{t} = \\frac{s (6 - rt - st)}{t} = \\frac{6s}{t} - \\frac{rts}{t} = 6 \\cdot \\frac{s}{t} - (6 - rs - rt),\n\\]\n\nbut a simpler way to see it is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r s^2}{t} = \\frac{r s \\cdot s}{t} = \\frac{s (5 - r - t)}{1} = 5s - rs - st.\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{s t^2}{r} = 5t - st - tr,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{t r^2}{s} = 5r - rt - tr.\n\\]\n\nAdding these three expressions together, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{r s}{t} + \\frac{s t}{r} + \\frac{t r}{s} = (5s - rs - st) + (5t - st - tr) + (5r - rt - tr).\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we have:\n\n\\[\n5s - rs - st + 5t - st - tr + 5r - rt - tr = 5(s + t + r) - (rs + rt + st).\n\\]\n\nSince \\(s + t + r = 5\\), we substitute this into the equation:\n\n\\[\n5(5) - 6 = 25 - 6 = 19.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\frac{rs}{t} + \\frac{st}{r} + \\frac{tr}{s}\\) is \\(\\boxed{19}\\).",
